CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ is_constructible via template move converting ctor: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [meta.unary.prop]: is_constructible<T, Args...> is true iff
`T t(declval<Args>()...)` is well-formed.  For T = pair<const int,int> with a
template move converting ctor `pair(pair<U1,U2>&&)` and Args = pair<int,int>&&,
the trait is TRUE.  Fixed in cpp_typecheckt's __is_constructible: build the
source expression from the de-referenced argument type (a reference-typed source
did not bind to an rvalue-reference converting-constructor parameter during
implicit_conversion_sequence).  Reduced from preprocessed <utility>/<type_traits>
via cvise.  Non-vacuous (assertion 2 must FAIL).
